Background Color for Pages:
#1A2A3A (Dark Blue-gray) – A bit lighter and softer, creates a nice contrast without being too harsh.
#F5F7FA (Light Gray) – A clean and neutral option for readability, providing a modern, airy feel.
#EAEAEA (Very Light Gray) – A soft, subtle backdrop that would allow other colors to pop, especially text and links.
#192734 (Dark Navy) – Slightly lighter than the footer, this keeps the color scheme consistent but still creates a visual hierarchy.
#3A4C63 (Muted Steel Blue) – Lighter and more muted, providing a professional, cool tone.
#253141 (Charcoal Navy) – Adds depth while maintaining the dark theme, but it’s a bit more neutral than the footer color.

Accent Colors:
#4CAF50 (Green) – A vibrant color for links or call-to-action buttons that contrasts well with dark tones.
#FFB74D (Warm Amber) – A contrasting warm accent color, giving a fresh and energetic vibe.
#F44336 (Red) – For highlighting important elements like error messages, alerts, or action buttons.
#009688 (Teal) – A calming and unique option for buttons, links, or other highlighted areas.

